ver (26 TAC §746.2203(b))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220709-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2805-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220709","date":"2022-07-09","original_code":"746.2805(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-08-01","finding":"Prohibited Punishments - Hitting with Hand or Instrument: This standard was evaluated in regards to a DFPS investigation.  An infant caregiver inappropriately disciplines the children by slapping them on the hand.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026681114","violation_type_title":"Prohibited Punishments - Hitting with Hand or Instrument (26 TAC §746.2805(4))","topic_label":"Other"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220709-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220709","date":"2022-07-09","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-08-01","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: An infant caregiver did not use good judgment when she slapped infants on the hands as a form of discipline.   A second caregiver did not demonstrate good judgment when she pulled children by the arm and handled children in a rough manner. This information was obtained through an abuse/neglect (DFPS) investigation.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026695411","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220709-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220709","date":"2022-07-09","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-09-16","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: Based on evidence gathered from a DFPS investigation, it is determined that caregivers did not exercise good judgement by failing to report inappropriate discipline and mishandling to children by a co worker. Caregivers stated that they witnessed this concerning mishandling on multiple occasions, and did not report their concerns.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026692625","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220709-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1003-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220709","date":"2022-07-09","original_code":"746.1003(3)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-08-01","finding":"Director Responsibilities - Employee Assignments: Based on information obtained in regards to a DFPS investigation, it is determined that caregivers are placed in classrooms and do not have the skills, abilities, or training to adequately manage the classroom.  This is evidenced by caregivers being overwhelmed.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026695410","violation_type_title":"Director Responsibilities - Employee Assignments (26 TAC §746.1003(3))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220709-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220709","date":"2022-07-09","original_code":"746.1201(2)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-09-16","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Relate to Children: Based on evidence gathered from a DFPS investigation, it is determined that a caregiver became frustrated with classroom conditions which resulted in the caregiver lifting an 18 month old off the ground by one arm causing bruising to the child's left arm.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026682442","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Relate to Children (26 TAC §746.1201(2))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220630","date":"2022-06-30","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905753054","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905753054","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-06-30","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220624","date":"2022-06-24","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905753053","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905753053","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-06-24","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220622","date":"2022-06-22","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":1,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905904655","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905904655","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-06-22","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220622-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-305-a-6","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-112075-i20220622","date":"2022-06-22","original_code":"746.305(a)(6)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"